{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And he called his name Jacob.</b> It was the Holy One, blessed be He, who called him, not his father. The reliable proof is the verse's saying (Genesis 25:26) ״וְיִצְחָק בֶּן שִׁשִּׁים״ — if Yitzchak himself were the one calling, it should have said ״וְהוּא בֶּן שִׁשִּׁים״ etc., since that is the form used when the narrator continues speaking about the same subject. Understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:16.773423103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}